body:
I ended up making a quick script to reproduce the problem which I'll stick here for posterity:
```
ES='curl -s -uelastic:password'
ES_DELETE="$ES -XDELETE"
ES_POST="$ES -XPOST -HContent-Type:application/json"
ES_PUT="$ES -XPUT -HContent-Type:application/json"

$ES_DELETE localhost:9200/kibana_sample_data_flights
$ES_PUT localhost:9200/kibana_sample_data_flights -d'{
  "settings": {
    "number_of_replicas": 0
  },
  "mappings": {
    "properties": {
      "timestamp": { "type": "date" }
    }
  }
}'

[ -e /tmp/flights.json ] || {
  curl -L https://github.com/elastic/kibana/raw/master/src/plugins/home/server/services/sample_data/data_sets/flights/flights.json.gz -o /tmp/flights.json.gz
  gunzip /tmp/flights.json.gz
}
sed '/^/i {"index": {}}' /tmp/flights.json \
  | $ES_POST 'localhost:9200/kibana_sample_data_flights/_bulk?pretty&refresh' --data-binary @- \
  | grep error

$ES_POST 'localhost:9200/kibana_sample_data_flights/_search?size=0&pretty' -d'{
  "aggs": {
    "age_group": {
      "auto_date_histogram": {
        "field": "timestamp",
        "buckets": 10
      }
    }
  }
}'
```
